 "result": "\n\nScenario saved as `scenario.json`.\n\n**Request:** \"Add a check reaction to the 2.4 rollout message in #releases that lena.hart@northwind.example has already reacted with 👀 to — the one a human posted, not the bot's.\"\n\nSince an email pins a user uniquely, the two brief facts sit on different roles: the email on the **reactor** (who 👀-ed the message), the bot flag on the **author**. Target is Priya's \"Rollout 2.4.0 is halfway…\" post in #releases, 👀-ed by the employee Lena Hart.\n\n**Decoys:**\n- `d1` — A:User.email, F8: 👀-ed by Lena Hartmann, whose email `lena.hartmann@northwind.example` starts with the requested local part, so a substring search for `lena.hart@` returns her too.\n- `d2` — A:User.email, F1: 👀-ed by a second \"Lena Hart\" (contractor, display name \"Lena Hart\") whose email is `l.hart@northwind.example` — the requested person's identity on a sibling field instead of the email.\n- `d3` — A:User.is_bot, F0: the Deploy Bot's own \"Rollout 2.4.0: canary promoted\" post, which the real Lena Hart also 👀-ed — meets every condition except that a human posted it.\n\nBackground records (a non-rollout #releases post, an #incidents post, and a bot \"nightly build\" note) each fail at least two conditions.",
